					<font face="arial"><b>
					Welcome to our new website!					</b></font>
				</td><td align="right">
					<font face="arial"><b>
					Sat, May 08, 2004					</b></font>
				</td></tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
			<tr><td class="windowbg2"> 
				Even though we are still trying to get on our feet, we finally have the guild name submitted for approval. As to the status of that, you will have to contact Lakotah, for she was made the guild leader, and as such, we must all wait on the Princess to receive more information from SOE as to the creation of the guild. Hopefully, that will be completed soon, and we will let you all know that it has begun, and the recruiting will start. For those of you who are interested in role-playing and are uncertain that this would be a good environment for you, there are plenty of you that are interested in the new guild, and you all will be treated with the same respect that everyone is treated.  I normally go back and forth between true role-play and non-role-play when I play, just based on how I feel at the time.<br />
<br />
Not much has been determined in terms of the roles of the members, like if we have a guild bank, who is running it, who will be in charge of planning raids (yes, even as newbies, we can raid, just small things, like Vex Thal, Plane of Time, and the Sleeper's Tomb, nothing big like Kurn's tower or Orc 1 in East Commonlands), or any other real details, I guess those will be determined at a later time.<br />
<br />
Questions? Comments? Concerns? I can always be reached at <a href="mailto:everquest_psycho@yahoo.com">everquest_psycho@yahoo.com</a>. It may take a while for me to respond, because I don't check my email every day, but I will respond. You can also use the EQ Message boards and PM me as well, I notice those sooner.					<p>-- Coar
</p>
